  "generated_text": "To solve this problem, we will set up a system of equations based on the information given. Let's define the variables first:\n\n- Let \\( x \\) be the number of questions Frank answered correctly.\n- Let \\( y \\) be the number of questions Frank answered incorrectly.\n- Let \\( z \\) be the number of questions Frank left unanswered.\n\nFrom the problem, we know the following:\n1. Frank answered 80 questions in total.\n2. Frank scored 232 points.\n3. Each correct answer is worth 5 points.\n4. Each incorrect answer is worth -2 points.\n5. Each unanswered question is worth 0 points.\n\nWe can write the following equations based on this information:\n\n1. \\( x + y + z = 80 \\) (total number of questions)\n2. \\( 5x - 2y = 232 \\) (total points scored)\n\nSince Frank answered 80 questions, we also have:\n\\[ x + y = 80 \\]\n\nWe can use the second equation \\( x + y + z = 80 \\) to express \\( z \\) in terms of \\( x \\) and \\( y \\):\n\\[ z = 80 - (x + y) = 80 - 80 = 0 \\]\n\nNow, we substitute \\( z = 0 \\) into the equations:\n\\[ x + y = 80 \\]\n\\[ 5x - 2y = 232 \\]\n\nWe can solve these equations step by step. First, solve the first equation for \\( y \\):\n\\[ y = 80 - x \\]\n\nNext, substitute \\( y = 80 - x \\) into the second equation:\n\\[ 5x - 2(80 - x) = 232 \\]\n\\[ 5x - 160 + 2x = 232 \\]\n\\[ 7x - 160 = 232 \\]\n\\[ 7x = 392 \\]\n\\[ x = 56 \\]\n\nNow that we have \\( x = 56 \\), we can find \\( y \\):\n\\[ y = 80 - x = 80 - 56 = 24 \\]\n\nSo, Frank answered \\( 56 \\) questions correctly. To verify, we can check the points:\n\\[ 5(56) - 2(24) = 280 - 48 = 232 \\]\n\nThe calculations are correct. Therefore, the number of questions Frank answered correctly is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{56}\n\\]",
